  "text": "[warm] The front door deserves its own dig, so we step off the core again. Seven captures, seven real commits — and every one still opens straight from the blob;  the plaque shows the one-line git command. [short pause] It was born a grid of cards that re-tiled at every ship.\n\n\nFive days in, someone drew it by hand. The source admits it: no layout engine — hand-placed. Within hours, the map began automating itself.\n\n\nTwo days later it had districts, slots, and a name: The Orrery Estate. [short pause] Then it hit the wall every map hits — density. Two philosophies fought here.\n\n\nThe Loupe: magnify, don't move.\n\n\nThe Fairground Gate: descend. The shipping commit stakes the claim: proving depth not a scorer tweak relieved the crowding.",
